<section class="section section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title section-title-center section-title-glow">Topics for expert commentary</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle section-subtitle-center">Steve is available for expert commentary, data quotes, and background interviews on the following topics.</p>
    <div class="outcome-grid" style="margin-top:32px;">
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>Salary negotiation</strong>
        <p>How much professionals leave on the table, when to counter, what "final offer" really means, and which levers matter most beyond base salary — equity, signing, title, remote policy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>Job search strategy</strong>
        <p>Why most job searches fail despite high effort, why 40–60% of $150K+ roles are filled before posting, and how a targeted search of 20 roles outperforms 200 undifferentiated applications.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>Executive hiring</strong>
        <p>What executive search firms actually evaluate before a first interview, how VP and C-suite candidates lose on positioning not qualifications, and what moves a hiring committee at the Director+ level.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>Resume and LinkedIn</strong>
        <p>How ATS systems actually work (vs. myths), what hiring managers look for in the first 8 seconds of a resume, and why most LinkedIn profiles signal the wrong level to recruiters and algorithms.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>Career transitions and layoffs</strong>
        <p>How professionals restart after a layoff, what the best severance negotiation strategies look like, and how to position a career gap in an interview without losing credibility.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <strong>The $100K–$350K professional labor market</strong>
        <p>Hiring trends, compensation benchmarks, what companies in tech, finance, and healthcare are actually paying for senior roles, and what data shows about supply/demand at the senior IC and executive level.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

